<<~ ahu slot=`#/bearing`>>
! Provenance and Publication ~ custody across transformations

An artistic source, a generated addition, an operator edit and a public derivative can share one final artifact without sharing authorship, rights or evidence. Publication is a distinct operation from creation. The Art Sigil's depicted scope governs the image-facing instruction; publication custody governs the records and credits traveling with the artifact.

This companion does not grant permission or invent licensing terms. Where rights are uncertain, label them uncertain and hold publication or seek authorization when necessary.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/roles`>>
!! Distinguish the contributors and their authority

* `originating source` — work or data to which a derivative refers; record creator and original source where established.
* `rights statement` — license, authorization, restrictions, attribution requirements, and the evidence supporting them. A file's availability alone grants no license.
* `visual references` — methods, examples, photos, and other inputs; their contribution roles are defined by [[Reference Roles|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/reference-roles]].
* `receiver contribution` — model or human-generated material; identify the action as generation, selection, interpretation, editing, typesetting or compositing as appropriate.
* `operator decisions` — accepted changes, refusals, hand edits, publication and distribution. An assistant's recommendation is not operator approval.
* `publication derivative` — a specific flattened/exported artifact with its dimensions, crop, color profile, embedded metadata (if any), and associated attribution and alt text.

These roles may overlap. They are not exhaustive ownership claims.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/release-card`>>
!! Release card ~ a companion record, not image-facing text

```toml
[work]
title = "descriptive human title"
source_id = "stable source reference or explicit unknown"
original_creator = "verified name or unknown"
permission = "documented scope and exact terms; not inferred"
transforms = ["annotated derivative", "independent composite", "export"]
editable_master = "path or identifier; preserve when authorized"
publication_image = "path or identifier; inspected separately"
credit = "actual required text and links, externally recorded"
alt_text = "independent visual description, checked against actual image"
platform_constraints = "actual known limits, crop policy, encoding"
release_authority = "operator or explicitly designated rights holder"
```

Reproduce required credits and URLs accurately in every relevant publication context. Do not assume an image's caption, embedded metadata, and visible plaque travel together: platforms may separate them. If the legal or licensing conditions require accompanying text, verify the delivery workflow rather than relying on aesthetic credit treatment alone.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/text-and-alt`>>
!! Typography, caption, alt text

Exact strings belong in a verifiable text-delivery requirement, even if a separate Art Sigil describes their visual hierarchy. Generative lettering may be visually compelling and factually wrong. Inspect exact strings after final export.

Alt text describes the actual image for its audience; it is not a substitute for source credit, and source credit is not a substitute for alt text. Both can accompany a public post. Avoid invented historical manufacturing claims when the visual result only simulates a print or painting.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/boundaries`>>
!! Limits and aftermath

* Artist-name resemblance does not establish authorship or a right to reproduce an artwork.
* An authenticated permission statement should not silently broaden from a specific use to all future uses.
* Source URLs remain outside the copyable Art Sigil unless a visible inscription itself is an intended pictorial feature.
* Platform formatting, character limits, cropping and link previews belong to release QA, and should be checked against actual publication conditions.
* A verified distribution artifact is not proof that it has been posted to an external account.
* Where provenance has unresolved conflicts, keep them visible and seek a ruling rather than filling them with plausible invented details.

The artistic and publication contracts may refer to the same work, but neither automatically authenticates the other.
<<~/ahu>>

